{"t": 8.804, "kind": "tool.result", "request_id": "r1", "actor": "super", "tool": "start_helper", "args": {"title": "5-slide deck about Uruguay", "brief": "Create a 5-slide presentation deck about Uruguay. Save it in the current working directory (/workspace) as a .pptx file named uruguay.pptx (use python-pptx if available; if not, fall back to a self-contained HTML slide deck uruguay.html). \n\nSlides:\n1. Title: \"Uruguay\" with subtitle like \"A small country with a big story\" \u2014 quick facts (capital Montevideo, population ~3.4M, official language Spanish, currency Uruguayan peso).\n2. History: Charr\u00faa indigenous people, Spanish/Portuguese colonial rivalry, independence 1825/1828 constitution 1830, early 20th-century welfare reforms under Jos\u00e9 Batlle y Ord\u00f3\u00f1ez, 1973\u20131985 military dictatorship, return to democracy.\n3. Culture: mate tradition, asado, candombe (Afro-Uruguayan drumming, UNESCO heritage), tango shared with Argentina, football passion (1930 first World Cup host & winner, 1950 Maracanazo).\n4. Economy & society: agriculture/beef exports, ~98% renewable electricity (wind, hydro), stable democracy, progressive laws (cannabis legalization 2013, same-sex marriage 2013), high literacy, Plan Ceibal one-laptop-per-child.\n5. Places to visit: Montevideo's Ciudad Vieja & Rambla, Colonia del Sacramento (UNESCO), Punta del Este, Cabo Polonio, Carmelo/Tannat wine country.\n\nKeep 3\u20135 concise bullets per slide, clean consistent design (e.g. Uruguay flag colors: sky blue, white, gold accent), readable fonts. Verify facts are accurate. When done, report the file path and a one-line summary of each slide."}, "result": {"started": true, "helper_id": "h1", "note": "The result will arrive as a message."}}
